d\u003C/text>\u003C/a>\u003Ca href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cap_Anamur\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"item-link\">\u003Ctext x=\"1034.4315789473685\" y=\"569.0955555555556\" fill=\"#DA8DBC\" font-size=\"14\">Cap Anamur impounded\u003C/text>\u003C/a>\u003Ca href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_Seiler\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"item-link\">\u003Ctext x=\"1223.8263157894735\" y=\"553.0955555555556\" fill=\"#DA8DBC\" font-size=\"14\">Arnold Abbott arrested\u003C/text>\u003C/a>\u003Ca href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iuventa_(ship)\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"item-link\">\u003Ctext x=\"1280.6447368421052\" y=\"537.0955555555556\" fill=\"#DA8DBC\" font-size=\"14\">Iuventa seized\u003C/text>\u003C/a>\u003Ca href=\"https://ooni.org/post/2019-blocking-abortion-rights-websites-women-on-waves-web/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"item-link\">\u003Ctext x=\"1318.5236842105262\" y=\"521.0955555555556\" fill=\"#9B9B9B\" font-size=\"14\">Women on Web blocked\u003C/text>\u003C/a>\u003Ca href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Privacy_concerns_with_Facebook\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"item-link\">\u003Ctext x=\"1375.3421052631577\" y=\"505.0955555555556\" fill=\"#9B9B9B\" font-size=\"14\">Facebook abortion case\u003C/text>\u003C/a>\u003Ca href=\"https://keepitfree.ai/it/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"item-link\">\u003Ctext x=\"1451.1\" y=\"489.0955555555556\" fill=\"#9B9B9B\" font-size=\"14\">A/I shut down\u003C/text>\u003C/a>\u003C/g>\u003C/svg>\u003C/div>\u003Cbr>\u003Cp>This graph traces the evolution of the terms &quot;\u003Ca href=\"https://books.google.com/ngrams/graph?content=mutual+aid&year_start=1950&year_end=2022&corpus=en&smoothing=3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mutual aid\u003C/a>&quot; and &quot;\u003Ca href=\"https://books.google.com/ngrams/graph?content=self-care&year_start=1950&year_end=2022&corpus=en&smoothing=3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">self-care\u003C/a>&quot; in the literature from 1950 to the present day. &quot;Mutual aid&quot; has been in decline for decades, while &quot;self-care&quot; has kept rising, overtaking it around 1980: care shifts from the group to the individual, something each person manages alone, through apps, platforms and protocols. Audre Lorde had described caring for oneself as \u003Ca href=\"https://www.are.na/block/4436850\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">&quot;an act of political warfare&quot;\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\n",false],"uses":{"params":["slug"]}}]}
